Covertype 
    Link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/31/covertype 
    Info: - ~580,000 rows with 54 features, classification of pixels into 7 forest cover types based on attributes such as elevation, aspect, slope, hillshade, soil-type, and more.
    AI Ops: Recommend Starting Set 

Poker Hand 
    Link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/158/poker+hand
    Info:  ~1,000,000 rows with 10 input features describing suit and ranking of cards
    AI Ops: Excellent for isolationg row scaling 

SUSY 
    Link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/279/susy
    Info: 5 million rows, 18 numerical features, Binary Classification and no missing values, made of distinguishing simulated supersymmetric-particle signals from background events
    AI Ops: Good for large scaling of rows

HIGGS 
    Link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/280/higgs
    Info:  11 million rows and 28 features, based around the HIGGS Boson and background processing
    AI Ops: Specifically designed as a machine-learning classification dataset (compressed CSV is around 2.6GB thought not a recommend starting point by any means)

Census Income KDD
    Link: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/117/census+income+kdd
    Info: ~300,000 rows with 40 variables, of weighted census data extracted from the 1994 and 1995 current population surveys conducted by the U.S. Census Bureau
    AI Ops: Realistic message dataset
    
